{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791358356926,"sessionID":"ses_eeab8ef93ffeNB11has6WTNJz3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"n7OBH2l5zuckCOoo","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1/candidate.py"},"output":"<path>/home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1/candidate.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"RSA pragmatic listener at depth 2 with a learned salience prior at the top.\n2: \n3: Extends the incumbent rsa_l1_salience to depth-2 pragmatic reasoning: a pragmatic\n4: listener L2 inverts a speaker who anticipates a depth-1 pragmatic listener L1.\n5: The listener's prior over objects is a softmax of salience weights (feature count\n6: and familiarization base rate) entering only L2's top-level inference. On\n7: uninformative prior trials, the choice reflects this salience prior.\n8: \"\"\"\n9: \n10: import jax.numpy as jnp\n11: import numpyro.distributions as dist\n12: from memo import memo\n13: \n14: from src.rsa.memo_kit import EPS, at, softmax_prior, vec, with_lapse\n15: \n16: PARAMS = {\n17:     \"alpha\": dist.LogNormal(0.0, 1.0),\n18:     \"w_features\": dist.Normal(0.0, 1.0),\n19:     \"w_familiar\": dist.Normal(0.0, 2.0),\n20:     \"lapse\": dist.Beta(1.0, 9.0),\n21: }\n22: \n23: \n24: @memo\n25: def L0[u: UTT, r: OBJ](lex: ...):\n26:     listener: knows(u)\n27:     listener: chooses(r in OBJ, wpp=at(lex, u, r))\n28:     return Pr[listener.r == r]\n29: \n30: \n31: @memo\n32: def L1[u: UTT, r: OBJ](alpha, lex: ...):\n33:     listener: thinks[\n34:         speaker: given(r in OBJ, wpp=1),\n35:         speaker: chooses(u in UTT, wpp=at(lex, u, r) * exp(alpha * log(L0[u, r](lex) + {EPS}))),\n36:     ]\n37:     listener: observes [speaker.u] is u\n38:     listener: chooses(r in OBJ, wpp=Pr[speaker.r == r])\n39:     return Pr[listener.r == r]\n40: \n41: \n42: @memo\n43: def L2[u: UTT, r: OBJ](alpha, lex: ..., prior: ...):\n44:     listener: thinks[\n45:         speaker: given(r in OBJ, wpp=vec(prior, r)),\n46:         speaker: chooses(u in UTT, wpp=at(lex, u, r) * exp(alpha * log(L1[u, r](alpha, lex) + {EPS}))),\n47:     ]\n48:     listener: observes [speaker.u] is u\n49:     listener: chooses(r in OBJ, wpp=Pr[speaker.r == r])\n50:     return Pr[listener.r == r]\n51: \n52: \n53: def choice_probs(params, ctx):\n54:     prior = softmax_prior(\n55:         params[\"w_features\"] * ctx.feature_count + params[\"w_familiar\"] * ctx.familiarization\n56:     )\n57:     heard = L2(params[\"alpha\"], ctx.lex, prior)[ctx.utterance]\n58:     return with_lapse(jnp.where(ctx.is_prior > 0, prior, heard), params[\"lapse\"])\n\n(End of file - total 58 lines)\n</content>\n\n<system-reminder>\nInstructions from: /home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1/CONTEXT.md\n# Context\n\n- Candidate directory (write your three files here): `data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1`\n- Responses (read-only): `data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/responses.csv`: 6703 forced-choice trials,\n  one row per click, from experiments E10_oddman, E1_dv, E2_manip_check, E3_ling_frame, E4_prior_frame, E5_baserate, E6_valence, E7_color, E8_levels, E9_twins, color_prior_rerun, levels_prior_action, sequences, size, speakers. Columns\n  include `experiment`, `condition`, `objects` (JSON list of 0/1 feature\n  lists, one per object), `feature_names`, `query` (`utterance` or\n  `prior`), `utterance` (feature index heard), `familiarization`,\n  `grayscale`, `framing`, `choice` (object index clicked), `participant_id`\n  and `trial_index`. You may analyse it (e.g. with pandas, from the shell) to\n  find what the current models miss; your model file may not read it.\n- Inner-loop round 1 of 1.\n- Self-check: `/home/user/auto-psych/.venv/bin/python3 -m src.rsa.loop.check_candidate data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1 --responses data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/responses.csv`\n  It takes 2-10 minutes (it compiles and fits your model). Give the shell\n  tool a timeout of 900000 milliseconds for it (the tool's\n  `timeout` parameter); with the default of 120 s the check is killed before it\n  prints anything. Run it once and read its result; do not re-run it unchanged.\n- Write and test your files **in your candidate directory only**: no drafts in\n  `/tmp`, the repository root or anywhere else. The loop reads only\n  `data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1`; a candidate.py anywhere else counts as no candidate.\n\n</system-reminder>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"RSA pragmatic listener at depth 2 with a learned salience prior at the top.\n\nExtends the incumbent rsa_l1_salience to depth-2 pragmatic reasoning: a pragmatic\nlistener L2 inverts a speaker who anticipates a depth-1 pragmatic listener L1.\nThe listener's prior over objects is a softmax of salience weights (feature count\nand familiarization base rate) entering only L2's top-level inference. On\nuninformative prior trials, the choice reflects this salience prior.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport numpyro.distributions as dist\nfrom memo import memo\n\nfrom src.rsa.memo_kit import EPS, at, softmax_prior, vec, with_lapse\n\nPARAMS = {\n    \"alpha\": dist.LogNormal(0.0, 1.0),\n    \"w_features\": dist.Normal(0.0, 1.0),\n    \"w_familiar\": dist.Normal(0.0, 2.0),\n    \"lapse\": dist.Beta(1.0, 9.0),","truncated":false,"loaded":["/home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1/CONTEXT.md"],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1/candidate.py","text":"\"\"\"RSA pragmatic listener at depth 2 with a learned salience prior at the top.\n\nExtends the incumbent rsa_l1_salience to depth-2 pragmatic reasoning: a pragmatic\nlistener L2 inverts a speaker who anticipates a depth-1 pragmatic listener L1.\nThe listener's prior over objects is a softmax of salience weights (feature count\nand familiarization base rate) entering only L2's top-level inference. On\nuninformative prior trials, the choice reflects this salience prior.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport numpyro.distributions as dist\nfrom memo import memo\n\nfrom src.rsa.memo_kit import EPS, at, softmax_prior, vec, with_lapse\n\nPARAMS = {\n    \"alpha\": dist.LogNormal(0.0, 1.0),\n    \"w_features\": dist.Normal(0.0, 1.0),\n    \"w_familiar\": dist.Normal(0.0, 2.0),\n    \"lapse\": dist.Beta(1.0, 9.0),\n}\n\n\n@memo\ndef L0[u: UTT, r: OBJ](lex: ...):\n    listener: knows(u)\n    listener: chooses(r in OBJ, wpp=at(lex, u, r))\n    return Pr[listener.r == r]\n\n\n@memo\ndef L1[u: UTT, r: OBJ](alpha, lex: ...):\n    listener: thinks[\n        speaker: given(r in OBJ, wpp=1),\n        speaker: chooses(u in UTT, wpp=at(lex, u, r) * exp(alpha * log(L0[u, r](lex) + {EPS}))),\n    ]\n    listener: observes [speaker.u] is u\n    listener: chooses(r in OBJ, wpp=Pr[speaker.r == r])\n    return Pr[listener.r == r]\n\n\n@memo\ndef L2[u: UTT, r: OBJ](alpha, lex: ..., prior: ...):\n    listener: thinks[\n        speaker: given(r in OBJ, wpp=vec(prior, r)),\n        speaker: chooses(u in UTT, wpp=at(lex, u, r) * exp(alpha * log(L1[u, r](alpha, lex) + {EPS}))),\n    ]\n    listener: observes [speaker.u] is u\n    listener: chooses(r in OBJ, wpp=Pr[speaker.r == r])\n    return Pr[listener.r == r]\n\n\ndef choice_probs(params, ctx):\n    prior = softmax_prior(\n        params[\"w_features\"] * ctx.feature_count + params[\"w_familiar\"] * ctx.familiarization\n    )\n    heard = L2(params[\"alpha\"], ctx.lex, prior)[ctx.utterance]\n    return with_lapse(jnp.where(ctx.is_prior > 0, prior, heard), params[\"lapse\"])","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":58,"totalLines":58,"truncated":false}},"title":"data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1/candidate.py","time":{"start":1791358356688,"end":1791358356918}},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}},"id":"prt_115474cc50011XEk6thRQTOY82","sessionID":"ses_eeab8ef93ffeNB11has6WTNJz3","messageID":"msg_115473be1001hKejd6r1byL0VV"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791358357099,"sessionID":"ses_eeab8ef93ffeNB11has6WTNJz3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"mKvRsoapDF5pH0Ui","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1/hypothesis.md"},"output":"<path>/home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1/hypothesis.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: Listeners reason at depth 2 by inverting a speaker who anticipates a depth-1 pragmatic listener, combining recursive pragmatic reasoning with a salience prior over referents. The salience prior, shaped by visual feature complexity and familiarization base rates, enters only the pragmatic listener's top-level inference and is not simulated in lower-level agents.\n\n(End of file - total 1 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"Listeners reason at depth 2 by inverting a speaker who anticipates a depth-1 pragmatic listener, combining recursive pragmatic reasoning with a salience prior over referents. The salience prior, shaped by visual feature complexity and familiarization base rates, enters only the pragmatic listener's top-level inference and is not simulated in lower-level agents.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1/hypothesis.md","text":"Listeners reason at depth 2 by inverting a speaker who anticipates a depth-1 pragmatic listener, combining recursive pragmatic reasoning with a salience prior over referents. The salience prior, shaped by visual feature complexity and familiarization base rates, enters only the pragmatic listener's top-level inference and is not simulated in lower-level agents.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":1,"totalLines":1,"truncated":false}},"title":"data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_2_repair_1/hypothesis.md","time":{"start":1791358356986,"end":1791358357091}},"id":"prt_115474df0001Ws1LLL